            <ArticleTitle>HAE therapies: past present and future.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>23</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1186/1710-1492-6-23</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Advances in understanding the pathophysiology and mechanism of swelling in hereditary angioedema (HAE) has resulted in the development of multiple new drugs for the acute and prophylactic treatment of patients with HAE. This review will recap the past treatment options, review the new current treatment options, and discuss potential future treatment options for patients with HAE.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
